summary:
  The quiet swap goes back to admitting only members whose delay moved,
  so a channel-only change (L/R/M) on a live wired member never reaches
  its loopback.

history:
  Found 2026-09-05 reading setDeviceChannel: the click writes the map,
  bumps _chanRev and restarts syncOffsetDebounce, which takes the quiet
  swap. The swap compared wanted and deployed DELAYS and skipped every
  member within 2 ms — a channel change moves no delay, so toSwap came
  back empty and the swap answered "deferred". The speaker kept playing
  full stereo until some unrelated rebuild happened to reload it, and the
  popup showed the L it had never been given. The swap now remembers the
  channel each loopback was built with and treats a changed one as a
  reason to swap; this mutant forgets the channel again.

target:
  package/contents/ui/SyncEngine.qml

find:
              if (Math.abs(want - have) < 2 && chWant === chHave) continue;

replace:
              if (Math.abs(want - have) < 2) continue;

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_syncengine.qml
  test_a_channel_change_on_a_wired_member_reaches_its_loopback: the swap
  must answer "swapped" and issue a PW_LBSWAP carrying channel_map=front-left
  for the wired member. Line-neutral.
